  "hints": [
    "Comparing `target` with the middle element tells you which half cannot contain it. Which half is that?",
    "Keep `lo` and `hi` so that the target, if present, is always in `nums[lo..hi]`. Loop while `lo <= hi`: check `mid = (lo + hi) // 2`, then move `lo = mid + 1` or `hi = mid - 1`.",
    "Finding a word in a printed dictionary works the same way: open near the middle, decide which half the word is in, and repeat on that half."
  ],
  "tests": [
